s"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga34_2006__ci03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"Whether translations and translators may be used in presbytery examinations is left to the presbytery's judgment as to whether qualifications are fully satisfied."}},{"id":"bco:19-3--case:cases/ga48_2021__2020-04.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga48_2021__2020-04.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Marusich v. Central Indiana Presbytery","year":2021,"disposition":"other","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga48_2021__2020-04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga48_2021__2020-04.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:19-3--case:cases/ga48_2021__2020-04.md:occ-8ddc720fab27","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga48_2021__2020-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga48_2021__2020-04.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":303},"excerpt":"a full and accurate record of its proceedings \" (See also BCO 19-3, 38-1,","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga48_2021__2020-04.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["BCO 31-2 investigation","strong presumption of guilt","investigative commission vs. committee","standard of review","great deference","BCO 39-3.3","indictment decision","record of proceedings","BCO 15-1","remand","sexual harassment allegations"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2020-4"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Marusich challenged Presbytery’s receipt of a commission’s finding that accusations against a teaching elder did not establish a strong presumption of guilt, and the commission’s failure to provide minutes or a full report. Without answering either issue or identifying an error, the SJC remanded for a new BCO 31-2 investigation, a narrative of the evidence, and a recommendation for Presbytery’s consideration under regular orders. The decision expressly establishes no general rule for BCO 31-2 investigations."}},{"id":"bco:19-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Mark Grasso et al. v. Philadelphia Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:19-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md:occ-6ada0f6b1041","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":139},"excerpt":"…and adopt” the doctrinal standards set forth in the WCF and its catechisms. (BCO 19-3, Q.2; BCO 21-5, Vow 2; BCO 24-6, Vow 2). In addition, officers ordained to office must further promise, of their own initiative, to inform their Presbytery (TEs) or…","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md"},{"id":"bco:19-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md:occ-7d75e8dd399e","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":141},"excerpt":"…posed to them for licensure make no mention of the form of government at all. (BCO 19-3).","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2008-01_2008-10.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["ordination","licensure","women deacons","stated difference","confessional subscription"],"case_numbers":["2008-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The Session of Crossroads Community Church challenged Philadelphia Presbytery's licensing and ordination of a candidate who stated a difference concerning women and the office of deacon but agreed to follow the BCO. The SJC denied the complaint and affirmed Presbytery's judgment; a dissent argued it should have been sustained."}},{"id":"bco:19-3--case:cases/ga29_2001__1999-07.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga29_2001__1999-07.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Jeffrey M. Black v. Eastern Carolina Presbytery","year":2001,"disposition":"not_sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga29_2001__1999-07.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga29_2001__1999-07.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:19-3--case:cases/ga29_2001__1999-07.md:occ-28a426cd2bd9","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga29_2001__1999-07.html","repository_path":"cases/ga29_2001__1999-07.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":304},"excerpt":"…license from Philadelphia Presbytery. The four constitutional questions from BCO 19-3 were then affirmed by the licentiate. The moderator prayed and addressed licentiate with the words of BCO 19-4. A motion was then made \"To record Mr. Ben Inman's…","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga29_2001__1999-07.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["creation days","Westminster Standards exception","transfer examination","exceptions to Westminster Standards"],"standard_of_review":"mixed","review_standards":["factual_findings","discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["1999-7"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Black challenged Presbytery’s handling of his complaint and its ruling that a licentiate’s non-24-hour creation-day view was not an exception to the Westminster Standards. The SJC denied remand because Presbytery had effectively adjudicated the complaint; the separate objection to proceeding without Black was not first filed below and was administratively out of order. It upheld Presbytery’s ruling that not every non-Calendar-Day view constitutes an exception. Because the record did not identify the licentiate’s precise view, the decision did not determine its acceptability or whether it could be taught."}},{"id":"bco:19-3--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/korean-southwest__233.html","record_id":"rpr_exception:rpr/exc/korean-southwest__233.html","type":"RPR exception","title":"Korean Southwest: Presbytery overstepped its constitutional authority in approving a church's request to inc","year":2025,"disposition":"raised","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/korean-southwest__233.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/korean-southwest__233.html","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:19-3--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/korean-southwest__233.html:occ-d642e860f9a0","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/korean-southwest__233.html","repository_path":"rpr/exc/korean-southwest__233.html","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/rpr_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/korean-southwest__233.html"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:19-3--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/south-coast__118.html","record_id":"rpr_exception:rpr/exc/south-coast__118.html","type":"RPR exception","title":"South Coast: No record of the questions for licensure being asked.","year":2025,"disposition":"raised","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/ex